  id: "S07-09", module: "C", topic: "A cylinder resting in a V-groove with faces at 60 degrees and 30 degrees: the force on the steeper face, which is the smaller of the two", diff: 3, rel: [["C", "Each face pushes perpendicular to itself, so the two normals are tilted away from the vertical by the angle each face makes with the horizontal"], ["C", "Resolving horizontally, the two horizontal components must cancel, which fixes the ratio of the two forces"], ["C", "Resolving vertically, the two vertical components must carry the whole weight"]], key: ["statics", "resolution", "normal reaction", "groove"], ans: 1, paper: "BANK-S07",
