  id: "S07-10", module: "D", topic: "A wheel rolling at constant speed: the acceleration of the point at the top of the rim, which is the same magnitude as at every other point", diff: 1, rel: [["D", "Every point of a rolling wheel moves in a circle about the centre, so every point has an acceleration of v²/r towards the centre"], ["D", "The centre itself does not accelerate, because the wheel rolls at constant speed"], ["A", "Separating the velocity of a point, which is a sum of the translational and rotational parts, from its acceleration, which is not"]], key: ["rolling", "centripetal", "acceleration", "top point"], ans: 3, paper: "BANK-S07",
